---@field SnowballCapacityPreference? aws.snowball.SnowballCapacity The Snow device capacity preference for this job, specified at job creation. In US regions, you can choose between 50 TB and 80 TB Snowballs. All other regions use 80 TB capacity Snowballs.
---@field Notification? aws.snowball.Notification The Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) notification settings associated with a specific job. The Notification object is returned as a part of the response syntax of the DescribeJob action in the JobMetadata data type.
---@field DataTransferProgress? aws.snowball.DataTransfer A value that defines the real-time status of a Snow device's data transfer while the device is at Amazon Web Services. This data is only available while a job has a JobState value of InProgress, for both import and export jobs.
---@field JobLogInfo? aws.snowball.JobLogs Links to Amazon S3 presigned URLs for the job report and logs. For import jobs, the PDF job report becomes available at the end of the import process. For export jobs, your job report typically becomes available while the Snow device for your job part is being delivered to you.
---@field ClusterId? aws.snowball.String The 39-character ID for the cluster, for example CID123e4567-e89b-12d3-a456-426655440000.
---@field ForwardingAddressId? aws.snowball.AddressId The ID of the address that you want a job shipped to, after it will be shipped to its primary address. This field is not supported in most regions.
---@field TaxDocuments? aws.snowball.TaxDocuments The metadata associated with the tax documents required in your Amazon Web Services Region.
---@field DeviceConfiguration? aws.snowball.DeviceConfiguration
---@field RemoteManagement? aws.snowball.RemoteManagement Allows you to securely operate and manage Snowcone devices remotely from outside of your internal network. When set to INSTALLED_AUTOSTART, remote management will automatically be available when the device arrives at your location. Otherwise, you need to use the Snowball Client to manage the device.
---@field LongTermPricingId? aws.snowball.LongTermPricingId The ID of the long-term pricing type for the device.
---@field OnDeviceServiceConfiguration? aws.snowball.OnDeviceServiceConfiguration Represents metadata and configuration settings for services on an Amazon Web Services Snow Family device.
---@field ImpactLevel? aws.snowball.ImpactLevel The highest impact level of data that will be stored or processed on the device, provided at job creation.
---@field PickupDetails? aws.snowball.PickupDetails Information identifying the person picking up the device.
---@field SnowballId? aws.snowball.String Unique ID associated with a device.

